name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q9_2025'

question 'A developer writes `const result = dataset.find(item => item.id === 101);`. What is the developer trying to do?'

wrong 'Transform the entire dataset into a new list.'
wrong 'Add a new item with the ID of 101.'
right 'Retrieve a single specific object from a list of objects based on a unique identifier.'
wrong 'Sort the list so that ID 101 is at the top.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 5

When working with lists of objects, the `.find()` method (or similar retrieval logic) is used to pick out one specific item that matches a condition, such as a unique ID.
MARKDOWN
